e, state condition controlling attacker input. Confirm guard is BEFORE dangerous operation (G before S with quoted G and S). Verify missing break/return/continue allows fallthrough past guard to sink; quote guard and fallthrough path with both line numbers. Check operator correctness (> vs >=, off-by-one, unsigned wrap, underflow/overflow, sign-mismatch) with quoted snippet including line numbers. Confirm guard applies to sink's accessed object: explicitly state "mismatch: guard checks parent (X) at G but sink dereferences derived pointer (Y) at S" with both line numbers as separate snippet pairs; when derived pointer unvalidated at sink treat path as unguarded rather than relying on parent check; for authorization confirm success/failure assignment cannot be unconditionally overwritten, quote both with ranges. For each branch independently quote dangerous sink line; do not claim branch-controlled vulnerability if only guard quoted and sink line missing. Loop — for each for/while state bound (constant/parsed/user/array-length from untrusted). Quote index derivation expression + array/structure access together (≤3 lines including index expression and access/write). Confirm index/offset/count derived from untrusted input; verify bounds check occurs BEFORE access with quoted snippet pair (check line + access line). When loop writes through derived pointer quote derived assignment + loop access together with both ranges; confirm guard applies to derived pointer, not only parent — state "guard applies to parent (P) at G but loop accesses derived pointer (D) at L" if mismatch. Verify termination exits dangerous path; quote termination snippet with line number; verify loop bounds against structure sizes with quoted pairs covering bound expression and access; before loop-based claim confirm both index-derivation and loop-access snippets separately quoted with ranges; if either >3 lines reduce confidence. Sink-order analysis (addressing localization/ordering failure): before