ior is described; if no dangerous sink quoted, omit CWE entirely. Localization (addressing low loc-f1): snippet must contain sink line(s); include exact dereference/assignment/write lines; use ≤3 line ranges; include function name; if function/file unknown state null; for multi-branch cases quote each branch sink independently. Conservative verification (addressing over-labeling/precision failure — high FP from missing sink quotes, guard-object mismatches, unquoted derived-pointer validity): only claim vulnerability when both source and sink visible as quoted pairs, unguarded or guard misplaced/applying to wrong object, with specific line ranges; base reasoning only on given code; follow actual control flow; when guard checks parent but sink uses derived pointer state mismatch explicitly with both line numbers and treat derived-pointer path as unguarded — do not claim vulnerability solely on parent check; if ambiguous (snippet >3 lines, guard object differs from sink object, missing source/sink pair, full-function range, derived-pointer validity at sink never quoted, sink inferred not quoted, no CWE-assignable sink visible) prefer false over true and reduce confidence; set confidence proportional to evidence specificity — narrow range + snippet at both source and sink + correct guard-check = high (≥0.8); inference/full-range/guard-mismatch/missing sink quote/unquoted derived validity = moderate (0.4–0.7); missing source or missing sink or inferred sink or no quoted dangerous operation = low/false (≤0.35); emphasize absence of quoted derived-pointer validity check at sink is limitation not evidence; avoid inferring vulnerability from absence of guard alone when sink not quoted; require both source and sink quoted separately for every claim; when derived pointer access at sink not validated by quoted snippet at sink line treat as unguarded only if sink quoted, else do not claim vulnerability; specifically avoid assigning CWE or high confidence when only source quoted 